desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Template Explicit Unescape",
	title_zh: "检测到Template Explicit Unescape",
	type: vuln,
	level: middle,
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-template-explicit-unescape",
	risk: "Security",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `template-explicit-unescape` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/javascript/express/security/audit/xss/ejs/explicit-unescape.yaml).
Original message: Detected an explicit unescape in an EJS template, using '<%- ... %>' If external data can reach these locations, your application is exposed to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. Use '<%= ... %>' to escape this data. If you need escaping, ensure no external data can reach this location.

CWE: CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')
References:
- http://www.managerjs.com/blog/2015/05/will-ejs-escape-save-me-from-xss-sorta/
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos.ejs": <<<POS
<%-K%(1%>

POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${*.ejs}.pattern_regex(/<%-((?!include).)*?%>/) as $p0
${*.html}.pattern_regex(/<%-((?!include).)*?%>/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Template Explicit Unescape",
	title_zh: "检测到Template Explicit Unescape",
	message: "Template Explicit Unescape",
}
